VeridianOS: KAuth polkit backend: no moc include for a file without classes

Polkit1Backend.cpp includes "Polkit1Backend.moc", but the file declares
nothing for moc (its QObject classes and the plugin metadata are in
Polkit1Backend.h, covered by the moc_Polkit1Backend.cpp include next to
it), so AutoMoc printed "Polkit1Backend.cpp: note: No relevant classes
found. No output generated." The include is removed; no generated code
changes.

--- a/src/backends/polkit-1/Polkit1Backend.cpp
+++ b/src/backends/polkit-1/Polkit1Backend.cpp
@@ -246,6 +246,4 @@
 
 } // namespace Auth
 
-#include "Polkit1Backend.moc"
-
 #include "moc_Polkit1Backend.cpp"
